  "evidence": [
    "V125 exposes exactly ten owned gateway metadata columns through the existing non-login legacy reader and current group directory. No hash, replay envelope, provider bearer, HR data or extra role membership is exposed.",
    "Three actual migration tests exercise owner/peer/company eligibility, restricted role rights, exact projected columns, original retirement, parent purge and pg_dump/pg_restore with restored RLS.",
    "The raw lookup intentionally does not filter native parent: mismatched parent metadata fails mapping instead of being misrepresented as a missing gateway.",
    "Actual typed storage coverage distinguishes absent, live, wrong-parent and retired gateway heads and current eligibility. Mapping/error tests retain malformed row, cancellation, interruption, flag and failure classification.",
    "Focused18 and broad151 cases pass on the same8290 unchanged inputs; format and architecture pass. Recovery ceiling125 and future126 rejection pass all15 recovery tests.",
    "No failed gate for this increment. Owned test resources are closed."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This increment has no retained worker, shared DI, HTTP or Mobile product caller; metadata alone does not authorize activation or prove private SDK key ownership.",
    "Ignored retained-worker-next drafts contain admitted retained observation/readback/atomic completion plus tests and DI; they are unaccepted follow-on work. Do not overwrite later tracked fixes with those drafts.",
    "Continue retained worker and actual Synapse readback, explicit completed native replay, then durable Mobile old/new SDK/store/inbox/outbox/read/push ownership.",
    "Normal phone28, live8b40/schema116 pushON/SMTP OFF, Mobile3d85d569/hosted gates and Starter9959c1d remain current. All54 communications groups and actual Apple runtime remain open."
  ]
